From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:05:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 131/151] Line endings: pick LF or CRLF from a menu, current
 one checked, counts for mixed files
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A click on the status bar's line ending item no longer converts at once: it
opens a menu with LF (Unix) and CRLF (Windows), the file's own one checked.
Picking that one changes nothing. A mixed, CR or LFCR file gets a first line
with the counts of each kind ("Mixed: 120 LF, 3 CRLF") and neither checked;
picking one converts every line, in one undo step. A text without any line
break has LF checked, the ending its new lines get, and CRLF disabled.
Edit > Line endings shows the same entries.

After a conversion the status bar says "Converted to CRLF — Ctrl + Z to
undo" in place of the counts for 4 seconds, or until the next undo. The
per-kind counts come from the cached line ending scan.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

